Can there be a 3rd argument for `column_to_rownames` called "clobber" or something that allows you to overwrite existing rownames? 

Original function:
 ```
> tibble::column_to_rownames
function (.data, var = "rowname") 
{
    stopifnot(is.data.frame(.data))
    if (has_rownames(.data)) {
        cnd_signal(error_already_has_rownames())
    }
    if (!has_name(.data, var)) {
        cnd_signal(error_unknown_column_names(var))
    }
    .data <- as.data.frame(.data)
    rownames(.data) <- .data[[var]]
    .data[[var]] <- NULL
    .data
}
```

Something like this for clobbering existing rownames (default to false for consistent behavior)
```
> column_to_rownames
function (.data, var = "rowname", clobber = FALSE) 
{
    stopifnot(is.data.frame(.data))
    if(tibble::has_rownames(.data)) {
        if(!clobber){
            rlang::cnd_signal(error_already_has_rownames())
        }
    }
    if (!has_name(.data, var)) {
        cnd_signal(error_unknown_column_names(var))
    }
    .data <- as.data.frame(.data)
    rownames(.data) <- .data[[var]]
    .data[[var]] <- NULL
    .data
}
```

