Recall that #514 is what triggered most recent work on this, i.e. dealing with `as_tibble()` methods for time series, poly, matrix and table. They were still using base name repair.

It's possible that `as_tibble.ts()` should make an exception for a univariate `ts` and just give the single column the name `x`, as `as.data.frame.ts()` does. BTW, here's the code for `as.data.frame.ts()`:

``` r
function (x, ...) 
{
  if (is.matrix(x)) 
    as.data.frame.matrix(x, ...)
  else as.data.frame.vector(x, ...)
}
```

